### Public non-profit fan-content policy basis and applicability limits

Reference: GRYPHLINE's official guidelines dated 2026-02-03, published by Gryph Frontier PTE. LTD. and its affiliates: https://endfield.gryphline.com/zh-tw/news/4497 . The guidelines support creation, display, distribution and publication of fan works by individuals or unincorporated groups within qualifying non-profit fan activities, generally without prior contact. Charges must not exceed actual production costs; incorporated groups or out-of-scope activities require prior consultation.

The project's stated purpose is unofficial, personal, non-profit BAKER-style interface reconstruction; being free is not a substitute for rights verification. The guidelines also require respect for the work/characters, third-party lawful rights and relevant people. They prohibit impersonating official content or causing confusion with official products/projects, and content that directly copies or extracts official materials without evident creativity, as well as other unlawful, infringing or inappropriate content. The guidelines may change; interpretation and applicability judgments rest with the publisher. Read the complete guidelines rather than treating this summary as unconditional permission.

The guidelines do not individually authorize this inventory or specifically establish their applicability to these website assets or packaged UI slices. The overall engineering work and each extracted, cropped or recolored asset's distribution basis are addressed separately: this inventory does not claim that overall creative labor automatically qualifies every image, nor that using an icon alone disqualifies the entire project as a fan work. Independent website rights, screenshot authorship and specific redistribution permission remain unconfirmed. Non-commercial use, attribution and this NOTICE are not official per-asset authorization or a guarantee of redistribution rights.
